sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/aerobic-power-bound> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sustained mechanical power is bounded by oxygen delivery (Fick) times efficiency (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "Aerobic mechanical power is at most η E Q (Ca − Cv) ≤ η E Q Ca; sustained flight needing P_req requires η E Q Ca ≥ P_req; climb under aerobic supply is at most (η E Q Ca − P_req)/W; and if supply scales with size with a smaller exponent than demand, there is a size above which supply falls short." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Flight.lean) for the flying-fish audit and the physics thread's coupled simulator (hub items 3 and 4, 2026-10-31); hypotheses named, no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "P ≤ η E_O2 Q (Ca − Cv) ≤ η E_O2 Q Ca ; sustained flight ⇒ η E_O2 Q Ca ≥ P_req ; b_supply < 7/2 ⇒ ∃ L*" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **Sustained flight needs enough oxygen.** If flight at speed `v` needs `P_req = W v / (L/D)` and the sustained power is aerobic, then `P_req ≤ η E Q Ca`. -/
theorem sustained_flight_requires {W v LD P η E Q Ca Cv : ℝ} (hη : 0 ≤ η) (hE : 0 ≤ E) (hQ : 0 ≤ Q) (hCv : 0 ≤ Cv)
    (hsus : P ≤ aerobicPower η E Q Ca Cv) (hflight : powerRequired W v LD ≤ P) :
    powerRequired W v LD ≤ η * E * Q * Ca"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.aerobicPower" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.sustained_flight_requires", "Delphi.aerobic_le_Ca", "Delphi.aerobic_le_metabolic", "Delphi.sustained_le", "Delphi.climb_le_aerobic", "Delphi.powerLaw_crossover" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Fick's principle, the oxycaloric conversion, aerobic (not burst) power and 0 ≤ η ≤ 1 are named hypotheses; no physiological number for Exocoetidae is in any statement." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Fick: O2 delivered = Q (Ca − Cv); the oxycaloric equivalent E converts O2 to metabolic power; mechanical power is at most η times it; sustained power is aerobic (anaerobic bursts, oxygen debt, and the glide phase, which needs no muscle power, are outside); 0 ≤ Cv ≤ Ca, 0 ≤ η ≤ 1, Q, E ≥ 0; the supply exponent is whatever the physiology gives, not derived here. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Flight.lean>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aerobic-power-bound> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/aerobic-power-bound> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-aerobic-power-bound> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-aerobic-power-bound> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.sustained_flight_requires with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 3 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Flight.lean (206 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.sustained_flight_requires, Delphi.aerobic_le_Ca, Delphi.aerobic_le_metabolic, Delphi.sustained_le, Delphi.climb_le_aerobic, Delphi.powerLaw_crossover: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 3 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [aerobic-efficiency-above-one] Mutant: the hypothesis η ≤ 1 dropped (replaced by True) while the metabolic ceiling E Q Ca is kept; with η > 1 mechanical power could exceed metabolic power, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 1 error(s): Flight.lean:157:4: error: linarith failed to find a contradiction [aerobic-venous-term-wrong-way] Mutant: the venous term dropped the wrong way, claiming aerobic power is at most η E Q Cv (the venous content) instead of η E Q Ca; false whenever Ca > 2 Cv, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 3 error(s): Flight.lean:150:2: error: linarith failed to find a contradiction [crossover-exponent-reversed] Mutant: the crossover claimed when the supply exponent EXCEEDS the demand exponent (b₁ < b₂); then supply overtakes demand and no size limit exists, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 1 error(s): Flight.lean:188:33: error: linarith failed to find a contradiction Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/aerobic-power-bound> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Fick: O2 delivered = Q (Ca − Cv); the oxycaloric equivalent E converts O2 to metabolic power; mechanical power is at most η times it; sustained power is aerobic (anaerobic bursts, oxygen debt, and the glide phase, which needs no muscle power, are outside); 0 ≤ Cv ≤ Ca, 0 ≤ η ≤ 1, Q, E ≥ 0; the supply exponent is whatever the physiology gives, not derived here. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

